    "prompt": "You read one hand-drawn button for a landscape phone game controller.\nThe image is a finger drawing made on the phone screen, white ink on dark or dark ink on light.\nThe image is the player's whole controller pad. They just drew ONE new control inside this region (fractions of the image, origin top left): x=0.4, y=0.3, w=0.2, h=0.3. Read only the strokes inside that region and ignore everything outside it.\nControls: a circle, joystick, D-pad or cluster of arrows is ONE control of type \"stick\" whose rectangle covers the whole cluster; its action is \"steer\" if it is on the left half, else \"move\".\nA single arrow drawn on its own is a \"button\" with action left, right, up or down.\nA box, circle or shape with a word or symbol in it is a \"button\" (a drawn switch or slider is a \"toggle\"). Copy the written word exactly into label, in UPPERCASE (FIRE, LAND, PEW, DIG...). Use \"\" if nothing is written.\naction: the closest game action, or \"none\". Verbs with typical labels: shoot (SHOOT, FIRE, PEW, LASER); boost (BOOST, TURBO, NITRO, FAST); shield (SHIELD, BUBBLE, ARMOR, ARMOUR); blast (BLAST, BOMB, WIN, NUKE); invisible (INVISIBLE, CLOAK, GHOST, HIDE); shapeshift (SHAPESHIFT, MASK, DISGUISE, MORPH); teleport (TELEPORT, WARP, BLINK, PORTAL); heal (HEAL, REPAIR, POTION, MEDKIT); jump (JUMP, HOP, SPRING, LEAP); land (LAND, LANDING, TOUCHDOWN, DOCK); takeoff (TAKEOFF, TAKE OFF, LAUNCH, LIFTOFF); scan (SCAN, RADAR, EYE, SONAR); flare (FLARE, LIGHT, TORCH, LAMP); drill (DRILL, SAW, PICK, PICKAXE); dig (DIG, SHOVEL, SPADE, CLAW); drive (DRIVE, CAR, WHEELS, BIKE); fly (FLY, WINGS, JETPACK, HOVER); swim (SWIM, FINS, FLIPPERS, BOAT); grapple (GRAPPLE, HOOK, ROPE, MAGNET). Movement: left, right, up, down, forward, back, strafeleft, straferight, rise, sink. Meta: ready, view.\nReturn exactly that one control: its type, label and action."
